`DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM` — prevalence census, 2026-09-09.

**Qualifying coalitions were common in the tested slice: at least one was observed at 30/30 real anchors.** This is a within-world diagnostic estimate, not an across-world prevalence claim.

## Mechanism prevalence

| mechanism | anchors with >=1 | fraction of all anchors | physical events exposed | candidates generated |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| Occupancy activation | 28/30 | 93.3% | 757 | 607 |
| Multi-aggressor relief | 0/30 | 0.0% | 0 | 0 |
| Complete beam evacuation | 29/30 | 96.7% | 534 | 534 |

Mechanism rows can overlap: a single physical assignment may be generated by more than one rule. The headline numerator is the union over mechanisms and therefore is not the sum of the rows.

Multi-aggressor relief had no trigger-eligible victim events in this slice, so its zero row reflects zero candidate exposure under the fixed rule as well as zero qualifying anchors.

## Energy-efficiency outcome

For the best qualifying coalition at each positive anchor, `EE(joint)/EE(anchor) - 1` was:

- minimum: **0.041561 (4.156%)**
- median: **0.091183 (9.118%)**
- maximum: **0.227558 (22.756%)**

The acceptance objective remained the sealed full objective `B - eta_ref E + kappa phi`; EE is reported separately as the owner-facing outcome and was not substituted into acceptance.

## Coalition sizes

- candidate coalitions tested by size: `{2: 922, 3: 215}`
- unique qualifying coalitions by size: `{2: 126, 3: 48}`
- best-per-positive-anchor coalitions by size: `{2: 18, 3: 12}`

## Occupancy exposure

Across 30 anchors there were **438 beam-anchor incidences at occupancy 1** and **319 at occupancy 2**, out of 1242 active beam-anchor incidences. Their shares were 35.3% and 25.7%, respectively.

## Coverage and search budget

- worlds: **1** (`V025_PROBE_R2/world/1`)
- anchors: **30** (30 per world)
- users per world: **100**
- base carrier: `nearest-eligible`
- objective field: corrected causal ACM, `realised` keyed fading, 48 boundaries, alpha=0.1
- unique joint candidate profiles tested: **1137**
- legal unilateral profiles evaluated to form matched marginals / fixed best alternatives: **2456**
- physical boundary evaluations: **175344**
- wall time: **1652.0 s**; concurrency: one process; nice level 10

This was a breadth-first, non-exhaustive census. A zero or low fraction means **rare within this budget**, not mathematically absent: only the three fixed physical-event constructions were tested, with one deterministic destination rule for relief/evacuation.

## Fixed rules and provenance

- Occupancy activation tested the two nearest legal arrivals into every occupancy-1/2 base beam.
- Multi-aggressor relief tested top-2 and top-3 aggressor-user sets only for interference-limited victims whose largest aggressor alone did not clear every decision-instant victim slot.
- Complete evacuation tested every occupancy-2/3 base beam; all occupants moved.
- For already physically selected relief/evacuation members, the destination was that user's highest decision-instant nominal wanted-link-margin legal alternative, with a stable physical-ID tie-break. Users and coalitions were never ranked by `|d_i|`; outcomes did not choose destinations.
